# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit game data. Belt and braces: none of this is in the tree today and
# these patterns are here to keep it that way.
#
# The cartridge dump is WaterMelon's commercial product and Paprium is still on
# sale. The music blob is decoded from the released soundtrack - raw 48 kHz
# stereo PCM, so it plays in any media player, which makes it an album rather
# than a game asset. Users supply both themselves; scripts/build_cdda*.sh
# rebuilds the blob bit-identically from your own copy.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pcm
Paprium.md
paprium.bin
*.sav
*.srm
sfx-dump/
cdda/
cdda-blob/
